      "id": "jobtracker",
      "title": "JobTracker",
      "description": "Track applications, follow-ups and job-search progress with Google Sheets as the database.",
      "longDescription": "JobTracker is a modern interface for my Switzerland job-application tracker. The Google Sheet remains the single source of truth: the app reads it, renders it beautifully, and writes changes straight back through the Google Sheets API using browser-only OAuth (Google Identity Services) \u2014 no backend, no database, no server. It handles the messy real-world sheet gracefully: mixed date formats, typos like 'Hybird', and hidden =HYPERLINK() formulas are all parsed correctly, while formula columns are never overwritten. An analytics dashboard adds KPIs and charts for applications over time, status breakdown, top locations and work modes.",
